    "created_at": "2026-04-23T17:15:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-23T17:15:16Z",
    "body": "> Wouldn't `<link rel=\"alternative\" type=\"text/markdown\" href=\"page.md\">` be sufficient?\n\nYes, great point. The existing `<link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/markdown\">` pattern was considered. While technically functional, `rel=\"alternate\"` is semantically defined as an alternative representation of the same content. The `ai:context` resource is intentionally not an alternative representation, it contains agent-specific context, constraints, and data that is deliberately absent from the human-facing page. Reusing `rel=\"alternate\"` would conflate two distinct concepts and reduce discoverability for agents parsing the tag with intent-specific semantics in mind.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
