    "created_at": "2026-04-23T17:22:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-23T17:22:19Z",
    "body": "I think this is a dupe of https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11548, and https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10946. \n\nTo quote what I said in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10946:\n\n> If you want to create your own standard that differs from the existing item*, or aria-* namespaces, the HTML standard isn't the correct venue to discuss or progress this, I believe. External specifications can create their own defacto attribute namespaces without any requirements from the HTML standard (much like aria-* does).\n\nWe have a list of [standard metadata names](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#standard-metadata-names) but we would probably want an external spec to link to that demonstrates what are the allowed formats.\n\nI think this is the wrong venue to incubate this proposal, and instead encourage folk to explore other standards venues (maybe WICG?) to nail down a proposal, which may or may not need integration in the HTML standard. \n\nI'll close this, as there's nothing actionable here, and this is a duplicate of previously unactioned issues. If you disagree with this conclusion let me know, and of course you're still welcome to use the closed issue to discuss this further.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
