    "created_at": "2026-04-23T19:45:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-23T19:45:44Z",
    "body": "@dgautsch \n> it contains agent-specific context, constraints, and data that is deliberately absent from the human-facing page\n\nI believe you can achieve this goal by doing with something like `application/ai+markdown` MIME. This would not only work well for HTML `<link rel=alternate>` but also with HTTP `Accept` + `Content-Type` headers, eliminating the need to fetch HTML document in the first place.\n\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
